"prose": [
{
"from": 261,
"to": 264,
"text": "The block runs the formatter and the linter; each touched crate's units; the filtered new-case entries (each selects only this chunk's new cases: 0 on the untouched tree, read red-vacuous at baseline); the integration binaries the chunk moves; the supply-chain bans (a dependency edge moves); the host read; the harness's three layers; then the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 266,
"to": 271,
"text": "**What is not run, and why:** no round and no live entry — R2 is the operator's act, outside this block, after implement's stop (`inputs#I1` item 5); no mutation run (`inputs#I1` item 10); no fuzz target (the new reads are a `clients` reply through the seam's existing parse, and closed words a bounded events read already parsed). The start gains a step only under `--origin` (a boot-path touchpoint, `start`): the harness boot smoke runs in the operator pass, unchanged in shape. The new test binary `tests/cli_open.rs` does not exist on the untouched tree, so no filter names it by `binary(…)`: its cases are selected by `test(/^open_/)`."
},
{
"from": 273,
"to": 275,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries, each fired on its own filtered entry, its case named, `--timeout 900`; each case fails on its own bounded assertion, so a `timeout` reading would NOT read the guard as held."
},
{
"from": 277,
"to": 281,
"text": "| id | File | The edit removes | Case | Entry | |---|---|---|---|---| | `open-allowlist` | `src/cmd/open.rs` | the `claude`-alone check in `checked` | `open_args_refuse_a_word_after_dashes_other_than_claude` | `ctl-root` | | `window-launch` | `crates/viola-state/src/replay.rs` | the clear of the held window on a `launch` line | `window_rule_a_later_launch_clears_it` | `ctl-state` | | `place-only-seen` | `src/run/window.rs` | the `pid == terminal_pid` match (the first client taken) | `window_step_with_no_window_is_window_unseen` | `ctl-root` |"
}
],
